{"id": "EUVD-2026-76431", "enisaUuid": "cdfb6647-4c86-30eb-8f07-1a5c3c8d1f16", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nudf: reject VAT indexes equal to the entry count\n\nUDF 1.50 virtual partition mapping uses the VAT as an array of physical\nblock mappings. s_num_entries stores the number of entries in that array,\nnot the highest valid index. The valid VAT indexes are therefore below\ns_num_entries.\n\nudf_get_pblock_virt15() currently rejects only indexes greater than\ns_num_entries. A crafted image can request index s_num_entries, pass the\nbounds check, and make the kernel read one entry past the allocated VAT table.\n\nChange the check to reject block >= s_num_entries, so the count is handled as\nan exclusive upper bound.\n\nA crafted UDF image reproduced this on origin/master commit\n0e35b9b6ec0ffcc5e23cbdec09f5c622ad532b53 with a KASAN slab-out-of-bounds\nreport in udf_get_pblock_virt15().\n\nTrail of Bits has a reproducer that triggers kernel panic demonstrating the bug, and can share it if needed.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:44:06", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:48:16", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f64e01a90326bb85a3cc8aa0199931dc2f15b589", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8a8c1c42a34349a0626d910abbad5a29136446b7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/19f36c6453cd88fe6d60ef36ab1f1cad8ddf4ce4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b77b83f5529a26d084d64ece98abd6f0cc86e053", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9193368408d792cec2057628d87862140fb1ce1c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b95c33a4e743874f1b0a45bf2aaa4da553552bd1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1bd7947f1463c21edafa256d0fbec5b99215e2b6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cac0cb07f29ccfb373fd4a36c81e908ef3ce608c"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-89525", "GHSA-383p-4f3r-q68w"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0506dcfd-f57f-3240-b22e-bc1527299622", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "0676c8a5-2c1c-387f-8245-c79414a7aa97", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.157"}, {"id": "263be598-7ae2-3a07-9433-feecf2981025", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <1bd7947f1463c21edafa256d0fbec5b99215e2b6"}, {"id": "2df37f7d-a058-350f-aeac-6e9b540840ef", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <b77b83f5529a26d084d64ece98abd6f0cc86e053"}, {"id": "3c7f7af9-bd0f-3b86-9b9d-76ef7c4ac259", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2.6.12"}, {"id": "4729187f-d92a-38a8-ac8b-4d8fa36bbab4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <9193368408d792cec2057628d87862140fb1ce1c"}, {"id": "49711df9-109b-3c82-93a3-1cf1ad55197a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.50"}, {"id": "49888310-3203-3fd7-8d84-bb0ae5eee20c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <f64e01a90326bb85a3cc8aa0199931dc2f15b589"}, {"id": "5e539a01-4a8d-3107-97ce-31293a50706f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <8a8c1c42a34349a0626d910abbad5a29136446b7"}, {"id": "78052deb-23c3-3c77-85a0-a438be68d348", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.270"}, {"id": "8b91f498-d8e7-3939-bfa4-a18dd0bea054", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.4"}, {"id": "a09e74fd-8a9d-399b-97b7-c3774ade2a93", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.221"}, {"id": "b8906fd4-0024-3868-a135-50f57cf0fa8